# E-1211: Let $\mathbb{N}=A\cup B$ where $A$ and $B$ are disjoint. Let $S(A)$ be those integers which are the sum of finitely many distinct elements of $A$, and similarly for $S(B)$. If\[\overline{\delta}(X)=\limsup_{x\to \infty}\frac{1}{\log x}\sum_{\substack{n\in X\\ n<x}}\frac{1}{n}\]is the upper logarithmic density of $X$ then how large must\[\max(\overline{\delta}(S(A)),\overline{\delta}(S(B)))\]be?
